        prognosis: 'Untreated: 7x stroke risk, 3x MI risk, reduced life expectancy by 10 years. Treated: Near-normal life expectancy. Good control (BP <140/90): Reduces stroke by 35-40%, MI by 20-25%. Resistant hypertension: 10-20%, higher CVD risk. Lifestyle modification: Can normalize BP in 50% of stage 1.',
        
        keywords: ["hypertension", "high-BP", "ACEi", "amlodipine", "cardiovascular-disease"],
        
        relatedConditions: ["stroke", "acs", "heart-failure", "ckd", "diabetes", "af"]
